<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="67974" href="schedule/2018/spring/ITAL/390/67974.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2018" href="schedule/2018.xml">2018</calendarYear><term id="120181" href="schedule/2018/spring.xml">Spring 2018</term><subject id="ITAL" href="schedule/2018/spring/ITAL.xml">Italian</subject><course id="390" href="schedule/2018/spring/ITAL/390.xml">Spec Topics Italian Studies</course></parents><sectionNumber>RS </sectionNumber><sectionTitle>Mediterranean Migration NGOs</sectionTitle><sectionDateRange>Meets 12-Mar-18 - 02-May-18.</sectionDateRange><creditHours>3 hours</creditHours><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>Migration in the Mediterranean: The Role of NGOs  The course focuses on the role of state institutions and NGOs as cultural mediators for migrants in and from the Mediterranean. This course will include a field experience in Pavia, Italy, May 25-June 9. During our time in Italy, we will meet with a number of NGOs and Italian state representatives to learn about how the migration emergency is managed from the perspective of cultural communication and mediation.</sectionText><partOfTerm>B</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>UNKNOWN</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2018-03-12Z</startDate><endDate>2018-05-02Z</endDate><specialApproval>Instructor Approval Required</specialApproval><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="LCD">Lecture-Discussion</type><start>ARRANGED</start><instructors><instructor lastName="Rota" firstName="E">Rota, E</instructor><instructor lastName="Stoppino" firstName="E">Stoppino, E</instructor></instructors></meeting></meetings></ns2:section>